{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794560684854,"sessionID":"ses_e2bda6365ffe9SboL4EsHkThoV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d426f074001j3V4EA5ImK9yj6","sessionID":"ses_e2bda6365ffe9SboL4EsHkThoV","messageID":"msg_1d426c4c20015teGKRA4APPK9w","type":"tool","id":"call_c0ced0bca32049b7ba4b4b17","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"FLOOR|typed_recall_at_1|false_offer|attachedMetrics\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/scratch/before.txt","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"3:$ FLOOR\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:$ FLOOR\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"FLOOR|typed_recall_at_1|false_offer|attachedMetrics\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/scratch/before.txt\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794560684148,"end":1794560684854}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794560684860,"sessionID":"ses_e2bda6365ffe9SboL4EsHkThoV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d426ed6e002CnGMnYWV4zdPNd","sessionID":"ses_e2bda6365ffe9SboL4EsHkThoV","messageID":"msg_1d426c4c20015teGKRA4APPK9w","type":"tool","id":"call_4065551ffb9b4c668ff0a233","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"slurpfile|holdout\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/spec.md | head -30","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"49:- An advisory lane (WG5 to WG13): check engines and doctor workflows that report what they measure and print the repair they promise, a command baseline with no holdout row, session readers that fall back and open the path they checked, a capped subprocess, a complete bench matrix and docs that match the code.\n66:Every command ran on 2026-11-13 from the worktree root at `320e7b64d4`, read-only, while other workers edited phase 009 research files and the parent packet metadata. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`, `PL` is this phase's `scratch/planning/` and `P7` is `../007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch`. The probes in `PL` build and remove their own temporary trees. The holdout counts come from `id` and `split` only. No holdout prompt text was printed.\n74:$ node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'\n154:$ jq -n --slurpfile h <(jq -c 'select(.split==\"holdout\") | .id' $RA/command-prompts.jsonl) --slurpfile b $RA/command-routing-baseline.json -c '{holdout: ($h|length), rows: ([$b[0].rows | keys[] | select(. as $k | $h | index($k))] | length), attachedRows: ([$b[0].attachedMetrics.attachedRows | keys[] | select(. as $k | $h | index($k))] | length), typedRows: ([$b[0].attachedMetrics.typedRows | keys[] | select(. as $k | $h | index($k))] | length)}'\n155:{\"holdout\":44,\"rows\":44,\"attachedRows\":0,\"typedRows\":0}\n221:| `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `command-routing-baseline.json`, `ADV/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | Modify, Regenerate | No holdout row published |\n222:| `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | Modify | Inventory, exit 3, `offerReached`, arena and holdout sentences |\n254:| REQ-015 | No task prints holdout prompt text, starts a model session or writes under the home folder. `AGENTS.md`, every `package.json` and the parent `spec.md` are unchanged and no added code comment names a spec path, phase number, task id or finding id. |\n270:| REQ-026 | `iter5-P2-holdout-secondary-split-publication`: the capture leaves holdout rows out of `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows`, the slice test compares non-holdout rows and asserts no holdout id, and the recaptured baseline holds 0 holdout ids. |\n291:- **SC-004**: `rg -n \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**'` prints nothing after the rebuild, and the recaptured baseline holds 0 holdout ids where it held 44.\n302:| Dependency | WG2 changes attach outcomes before WG9 recaptures | The slice test drifts on a holdout aggregate between the two lanes | WG9 runs in wave 2 after WG2. T041 records the metrics delta of the capture against the committed file before it writes, and REQ-014 blocks a lower floor |\n323:- **NFR-S02**: No task prints holdout prompt text. Scripts count holdout rows by `id` and `split` only.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"49:- An advisory lane (WG5 to WG13): check engines and doctor workflows that report what they measure and print the repair they promise, a command baseline with no holdout row, session readers that fall back and open the path they checked, a capped subprocess, a complete bench matrix and docs that match the code.\n66:Every command ran on 2026-11-13 from the worktree root at `320e7b64d4`, read-only, while other workers edited phase 009 research files and the parent packet metadata. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`, `PL` is this phase's `scratch/planning/` and `P7` is `../007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch`. The probes in `PL` build and remove their own temporary trees. The holdout counts come from `id` and `split` only. No holdout prompt text was printed.\n74:$ node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'\n154:$ jq -n --slurpfile h <(jq -c 'select(.split==\"holdout\") | .id' $RA/command-prompts.jsonl) --slurpfile b $RA/command-routing-baseline.json -c '{holdout: ($h|length), rows: ([$b[0].rows | keys[] | select(. as $k | $h | index($k))] | length), attachedRows: ([$b[0].attachedMetrics.attachedRows | keys[] | select(. as $k | $h | index($k))] | length), typedRows: ([$b[0].attachedMetrics.typedRows | keys[] | select(. as $k | $h | index($k))] | length)}'\n155:{\"holdout\":44,\"rows\":44,\"attachedRows\":0,\"typedRows\":0}\n221:| `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `command-routing-baseline.json`, `ADV/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | Modify, Regenerate | No holdout row published |\n222:| `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | Modify | Inventory, exit 3, `offerReached`, arena and holdout sentences |\n254:| REQ-015 | No task prints holdout prompt text, starts a model session or writes under the home folder. `AGENTS.md`, every `package.json` and the parent `spec.md` are unchanged and no added code comment names a spec path, phase number, task id or finding id. |\n270:| REQ-026 | `iter5-P2-holdout-secondary-split-publication`: the capture leaves holdout rows out of `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows`, the slice test compares non-holdout rows and asserts no holdout id, and the recaptured baseline holds 0 holdout ids. |\n291:- **SC-004**: `rg -n \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**'` prints nothing after the rebuild, and the recaptured baseline holds 0 holdout ids where it held 44.\n302:| Dependency | WG2 changes attach outcomes before WG9 recaptures | The slice test drifts on a holdout aggregate between the two lanes | WG9 runs in wave 2 after WG2. T041 records the metrics delta of the capture against the committed file before it writes, and REQ-014 blocks a lower floor |\n323:- **NFR-S02**: No task prints holdout prompt text. Scripts count holdout rows by `id` and `split` only.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"slurpfile|holdout\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/spec.md | head -30\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794560683374,"end":1794560684860}}}}
